+## Review 8589cfb6ed499246 — tied-size branch is absent from normal lessons
+
+A bounded protected-Racket probe found that four normal generated
+demonstrations all have strictly distinct component sizes.  Therefore the
+executable rival “descending area, then descending color” fits every generated
+demo tested.  The official query has equal-size color-8 and color-9 components;
+the canonical top/left/color tie chain places color 8 first, while the rival
+places color 9 first.
+
+Evidence is retained in
+`counterexamples/review-8589cfb6ed499246-v0001/learnability.json` and
+`case.json`.  The generator source was not changed.  The next concrete repair
+is a normal non-degenerate profile with equal-area components whose color order
+disagrees with top-left order, plus a focused test of the complete tie chain.
+The finding covers four generated demos and one canonical query, not every
+possible lesson.
