+## Review 8589cfb6ed499246 — unconstrained demo windows can omit a rule branch
+
+For seed 22 at easy difficulty, sample indices 0–2 are all `count3_triad` and
+show only `top`, `bottom`, and `other`.  Sample index 3 is
+`eight_hole_pair` and introduces the unseen eight-cell branch.  Under protected
+Racket, an executable rival that changes only `count=8` from label 3 to label 4
+fits all three visible demonstrations and changes the query.
+
+Evidence is retained in
+`counterexamples/review-8589cfb6ed499246-v0001/learnability.json` and
+`case.json`.  The generator source was not changed.  The next concrete repair
+is branch-aware lesson assembly covering `one`, `eight`, `top`, `bottom`, and
+`other`, or a deterministic profile schedule rather than an unconstrained
+consecutive default window.  This is one bounded lesson and one branch-local
+rival, not a universal ambiguity claim.
